] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/316468"} "22 from 22 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Losing quarter-finalists compete against losing semi-finalist for bronze."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/106421"} "Lucie Décosse"] " (FRA) was silver medalist in this class at Beijing and was a three-time World Champion, including wins in 2010 and 2011, and came to London as the hot favorite. She dominated the class all day long, winning her first two matches by " [:em {} "ippon"] ", and then moving into the final with a win by penalties over Korean " [:a {:href "/athletes/124415"} "Hwang Ye-Seul"] ". There she met German " [:a {:href "/athletes/124801"} "Kerstin Thiele"] ", who was a surprise finalist. The final was another comfortable victory for Décosse who added the only trophy she was lacking. Décosse score a " [:em {} "waza-ari"] " early in the match and added two " [:em {} "yukos"] " near the end to win easily. Thiele had advanced by defeating second seeded " [:a {:href "/athletes/92381"} "Edith Bosch"] " (NED) in the quarter-finals, and then survived a tough semi-final against China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/122540"} "Chen Fei"] ". Bosch came back to win a bronze medal, joined by Colombian " [:a {:href "/athletes/112601"} "Yuri Alvear"] ", who defeated Chen for the bronze. For Bosch, it was her third Olympic medal, with a silver from 2004 and a bronze in 2008."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Bosch achieved further fame during London 2012 just before the start of the men’s 100 metre final in athletics. She was seated next to a drunken fan who threw a beer bottle onto the track just as the athletes were lining up. Bosch subdued the idiot until the police arrived to take him away."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athlet